WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.133
-Welcome, everybody.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.501
Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show"!

00:00:03.501 --> 00:00:05.200
You're here!
You're watching!

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:07.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.567 --> 00:00:09.868
We're indoors.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:09.868 --> 00:00:13.567
Yeah. It is scorching hot
outside today.

00:00:13.567 --> 00:00:15.400
Yeah, it's even hotter in here

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.200
because Ryan Gosling
is my guest tonight.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:22.434
-Oh!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:22.434 --> 00:00:23.901
-I'm so excited
that Ryan's here.

00:00:23.901 --> 00:00:25.567
I just hope that
we can patch up our friendship

00:00:25.567 --> 00:00:27.400
after he stole my look.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:31.000
[ Laughter ]
I was just...

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.968
Yep, Ryan's here to talk about
his new movie, "The Gray Man,"

00:00:33.968 --> 00:00:36.968
which comes out at Netflix --
at midnight tonight on Netflix.

00:00:36.968 --> 00:00:40.667
Yeah. The movie also stars
Regé-Jean Page...

00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:41.701
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:00:41.701 --> 00:00:43.667
...and Chris Evans.

00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:45.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:45.534 --> 00:00:47.334
So, if you have plans
with your girlfriend

00:00:47.334 --> 00:00:48.834
this weekend, you don't.

00:00:48.834 --> 00:00:51.100
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:53.234
Well, the big news is
still the extreme heat

00:00:53.234 --> 00:00:55.901
that continues to slam millions
of people across the world.

00:00:55.901 --> 00:00:57.367
I mean, it is so hot outside.

00:00:57.367 --> 00:00:59.200
This is crazy.
You're not gonna believe this.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:00.834
But everything in Times Square
is melted

00:01:00.834 --> 00:01:03.801
except the M&amp;M's Store.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.801 --> 00:01:06.367
Until one person puts it in
their mouth, then it's all over.

00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:07.467
-Not in their hand.

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:08.801
-Yeah, it is brutally hot
out there.

00:01:08.801 --> 00:01:10.334
Apparently,
we added a new season.

00:01:10.334 --> 00:01:13.300
Now there's fall, winter,
spring, summer, and air fryer.

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:15.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:16.634
I wish I could say the heat
is going to ease up,

00:01:16.634 --> 00:01:19.000
but the weekend forecast
looks even worse.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.534
Check this out.
On Friday, they're saying

00:01:20.534 --> 00:01:22.734
it's gonna be 97 degrees.

00:01:22.734 --> 00:01:25.701
Saturday, over 100.
[ Audience groans ]

00:01:25.701 --> 00:01:27.400
And on Sunday,
it's just a picture of the sun

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:28.501
giving the finger.
-Oh, my --

00:01:28.501 --> 00:01:30.033
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:30.033 --> 00:01:31.400
-Do you believe that?
-Double bird.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:32.567
-Isn't that insane?
The double bird.

00:01:32.567 --> 00:01:34.167
[ Applause ]

00:01:34.167 --> 00:01:35.701
-Wow.

00:01:35.701 --> 00:01:37.033
-Yeah, the country
is dealing with

00:01:37.033 --> 00:01:38.534
record-breaking temperatures.

00:01:38.534 --> 00:01:40.467
I saw that the local news
did a helpful story

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:42.400
about ways to beat the heat.
Listen to this.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:44.167
-And with the city
under a heat alert,

00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:46.601
experts are urging people
to keep safe.

00:01:46.601 --> 00:01:48.667
-Yeah, we've got some tips
to help you stay cool

00:01:48.667 --> 00:01:50.267
on hot days like today.

00:01:50.267 --> 00:01:52.467
If you can, you should avoid
the outdoors

00:01:52.467 --> 00:01:55.400
from 11:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m.,
stay hydrated,

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:57.234
put ice cubes on your nipples,

00:01:57.234 --> 00:01:59.767
limit the use of your oven,
yell, "Nothing!"

00:01:59.767 --> 00:02:01.033
when your wife walks in
and says,

00:02:01.033 --> 00:02:02.834
"What are you doing
with those ice cubes?"

00:02:02.834 --> 00:02:05.167
Frantically, pop the ice cubes
in your mouth and say,

00:02:05.167 --> 00:02:07.634
"I have to go...do our taxes."

00:02:07.634 --> 00:02:10.267
And finally, turn on
the A.C. if you got one.

00:02:10.267 --> 00:02:12.200
-Yeah. See?
There's good tips right there.

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:14.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.434
Switching gears.
Everyone's talking about this.

00:02:16.434 --> 00:02:18.234
Today, the White House announced
that President Biden

00:02:18.234 --> 00:02:20.968
has a mild case of COVID.

00:02:20.968 --> 00:02:22.834
On the bright side,
it's the first positive news

00:02:22.834 --> 00:02:26.467
Biden's gotten in months.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.467 --> 00:02:27.767
Hey, I read that, tomorrow,
former President Trump

00:02:27.767 --> 00:02:31.934
and Mike Pence are holding
dueling campaign events

00:02:31.934 --> 00:02:34.133
